  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Women and Youth to drive sustainable Agriculture in Juba, SSD</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam in South Sudan, with funding (1 million USD) from IBSA through United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), will be implementing a project titled &quot;Empowering Women and Youth to Drive Sustainable Agriculture in South Sudan.&quot; The project (R11184) aims at increasing the scale of production of vegetables for smallholder farmers in Juba. The project is a follow -up to the past implemented project (a Swedish International Development Agency (SIDA) -funded grant) targeting 200 women and youths in Juba, and this will enable youth and women -led vegetable producer groups to increase production, improve the quality of produce, and market the produce, thus geared towards stabilizing food and nutrition security and income for the smallholder farmers.</narrative>
  </description>
